      en: "Mount Niha is a 1,650-m peak in the western Lebanon Mountains, overlooking the Bekaa Valley. Its slopes are terraced for agriculture, growing olives, grapes, and apples. The mountain has a Mediterranean climate with hot dry summers and cool wet winters. Annual rainfall is about 900 mm. The area is geologically active, with numerous springs and sinkholes. The Roman temple of Niha, dating to the 1st century AD, is a major archaeological attraction.",
