      en: "The Naqoura coast is located at Lebanon's southernmost point, adjacent to the Israeli border. The shoreline extends about 5 km, with rocky cliffs and small pebble beaches. The area is part of the Tyre Coast Nature Reserve, which protects sea turtle nesting sites. The coastal waters are relatively undisturbed due to restricted access, supporting healthy fish populations. The underwater archaeology includes ancient shipwrecks. Political tensions have limited development, preserving the natural state of the coast.",
